4. LICENSE KEY USAGE

WaveShaper can be installed and used free of charge. Features marked
Premium in the Software require the purchase of a Premium license key.

A Premium license key is personal to one person:

  - A key may be used on up to 3 computers at the same time. You can
    release a computer in Arctisoft Studio Hub to use the license on
    another one. A computer that has not used the license for 45 days is
    released automatically.
  - Sharing, publishing or distributing your license key is prohibited.
  - A license may be passed on only as a whole, using the transfer
    function in Arctisoft Studio Hub. After a transfer you may no longer
    use it.
  - Keys that are misused or obtained by fraud may be deactivated.

The computers using a license are recorded solely to apply these limits,
not to track individual user activity. The License Agreement in Arctisoft
Studio Hub states the complete terms.


5. DATA HANDLING

WaveShaper stores minimal data on the server while all settings and audio
data remain local on your device.

What WaveShaper stores on the server:

  - Progress: Experience points and level (updated after each export)
  - Avatar: Your profile image (if uploaded)
  - License: Current license type and activation status

What WaveShaper stores locally:

  - Settings: EQ preferences, effect parameters, export configuration
  - Presets: Custom EQ presets and effect configurations
  - History: Recent projects, downloads, and export history

What WaveShaper does not store:

  - Names, emails, addresses, or phone numbers
  - Payment information (handled securely by Stripe)
  - The actual content of processed audio files
  - Your file system activity outside of WaveShaper

Privacy controls:

  - Delete individual history entries via right-click context menus.
  - Unlink your account via the application menu.
  - Factory reset to remove all local settings and data.

Data retention:

  - Basic accounts: Automatically deleted after 365 days of inactivity.
  - Premium accounts: Retained while license is active.


6. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

WaveShaper incorporates the following open-source libraries:

  NAudio 2.2.1       MIT          Audio decoding, playback, device I/O
  NAudio.Lame 2.1.0  MIT/LGPL     MP3 encoding via LAME encoder
  TagLibSharp 2.3.0  LGPL         Audio metadata reading and writing
  Newtonsoft.Json     MIT          JSON serialization for settings

Users should review and comply with the licensing terms of these components.


